1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:06,560
DIMNA: Kalila, if your best friend asked you to ride on his back across the sea, would you say yes?

2
00:00:06,710 --> 00:00:09,130
KALILA: Of course. A friend is a friend.

3
00:00:09,280 --> 00:00:14,430
DIMNA: Hmm. Even if your friend had a secret plan? Sit down, brother. Let me tell you a story.

4
00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:31,150
Once upon a time, an old monkey lived all alone in a big fig tree by the sea. He used to be the king of the monkeys, but now he was old, and a younger monkey had taken his place.

5
00:00:31,600 --> 00:00:35,370
MONKEY: Oh well. At least I have my tree, my figs, and the sea breeze.

6
00:00:36,970 --> 00:00:41,610
One sunny day, a tortoise swam up to the shore and rested under the fig tree.

7
00:00:42,560 --> 00:00:45,980
MONKEY: Hello down there! You look tired. Would you like a sweet fig?

8
00:00:47,430 --> 00:00:51,200
TORTOISE: A fig? For me? Oh, thank you, kind monkey!

9
00:00:52,800 --> 00:01:03,940
The tortoise came back the next day, and the next, and the next. The monkey threw down figs, the tortoise told stories of the sea, and they laughed and laughed. They became best friends.

10
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:11,670
But back home, on a little island, Mrs. Tortoise was not happy at all.

11
00:01:11,820 --> 00:01:15,670
MRS. TORTOISE: Every day you are with that monkey! You never stay home with me anymore.

12
00:01:15,820 --> 00:01:19,670
So she pretended to be very sick, and she said something terrible.

13
00:01:20,120 --> 00:01:24,550
MRS. TORTOISE: Oh, I feel so ill! The only thing that can make me well... is a monkey's heart!

14
00:01:26,350 --> 00:01:31,910
TORTOISE: A monkey's heart? But the monkey is my friend... Oh, what shall I do?

15
00:01:32,460 --> 00:01:36,730
The tortoise thought and thought. And then, sadly, he made a bad choice.

16
00:01:38,730 --> 00:01:46,650
TORTOISE: Dear friend, come to my island for a big dinner! Climb on my back, and I will carry you across the sea.

17
00:01:46,800 --> 00:01:49,440
MONKEY: A dinner party? How lovely! Let's go!

18
00:01:52,440 --> 00:01:57,910
So the monkey climbed onto the tortoise's back, and off they swam, over the deep blue sea.

19
00:02:00,510 --> 00:02:03,180
But in the middle of the sea, the tortoise stopped.

20
00:02:03,330 --> 00:02:11,040
TORTOISE: Friend, I must tell you the truth. My wife is sick, and she says only a monkey's heart can make her well.

21
00:02:11,490 --> 00:02:12,760
MONKEY: My heart?!

22
00:02:13,410 --> 00:02:19,220
The monkey was far from home, and he could not swim. But he did not panic. He used his head.

23
00:02:19,870 --> 00:02:27,610
MONKEY: Oh, silly friend, why didn't you tell me before? Monkeys never take their hearts on trips! I left mine hanging in my fig tree. Let's go back and get it!

24
00:02:29,610 --> 00:02:36,980
So the tortoise turned around and swam all the way back. The moment they reached the shore, the monkey leapt up into his tree.

25
00:02:37,930 --> 00:02:41,260
TORTOISE: Now, friend, bring your heart, and let's go!

26
00:02:41,410 --> 00:02:47,620
MONKEY: My heart was with me all along! A true friend would never trick me. Go home, tortoise. I will never ride on your back again.

27
00:02:48,270 --> 00:02:51,860
TORTOISE: Oh... I was wrong. I am sorry, my friend.

28
00:02:52,310 --> 00:02:58,460
And the tortoise swam home, sad, and a little bit wiser. He had lost the best friend he ever had.

29
00:03:01,260 --> 00:03:05,770
KALILA: So the monkey stayed calm, and he used his head to get home safe.

30
00:03:05,920 --> 00:03:11,600
DIMNA: And the tortoise learned: never trick a friend! A true friend uses their head, and trusts wisely.

31
00:03:12,150 --> 00:03:15,910
DIMNA: Persian word of the day! In Persian, a friend is doost. Doost!

32
00:03:16,060 --> 00:03:19,590
KALILA: Doost. A friend. Let's always be a good doost.

33
00:03:21,140 --> 00:03:25,370
KALILA: And next time: a ring-dove, her friends, and a hunter's net.

